2026-09-23T12:13:12.3883050Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3883442Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3883755Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3883923Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884125Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884284Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884478Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884642Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884864Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3884941Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885009Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885076Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885151Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885235Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885305Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885369Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885448Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885515Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885583Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885725Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885809Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885877Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3885952Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886022Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886141Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886279Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886352Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886526Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886612Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886691Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886770Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886837Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3886927Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3887055Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3887122Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3887293Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3887877Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3887949Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888020Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888091Z     Features
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888168Z     --------
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888236Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888604Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888772Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3888854Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889093Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889178Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889245Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889462Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889596Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889663Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889873Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3889966Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3890031Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3890119Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3890190Z     
2026-09-23T12:13:12.3890560Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
